 "summary": "A 12-week, 3-day beginner program that rotates four different full-body workouts, each with three main lifts and two accessories done as a descending-rep pyramid of three sets. This is the strength variation; the hypertrophy variation uses 5-8 / 8-12 / 12-15 on the main lifts, accessories are the same.",
 "evidenceNote": "Stopping 1-2 reps short of failure on every set fits current evidence for beginners, and the pyramid gives both heavy and moderate-rep exposure. Because four workouts rotate over three days, each main lift is trained less than once a week and most muscles get roughly 4-9 hard sets weekly, which is on the low side for hypertrophy but fine for new lifters. No deload or stall rule is given.",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "Greg Nuckols Beginner Program (Boostcamp, free program page, updated Oct 2026)",
   "url": "https://www.boostcamp.app/greg-nuckols/greg-nuckols-beginner-program",
   "kind": "article"
  },
  {
   "title": "Greg Nuckols Beginner Program - detailed program guide (Boostcamp)",
   "url": "https://www.boostcamp.app/greg-nuckols-beginner-program",
   "kind": "article"
  }
 ],
 "schedule": "3 non-consecutive days (Mon/Wed/Fri). Workouts A, B, C, D rotate continuously: week 1 A-B-C, week 2 D-A-B, week 3 C-D-A, and so on for 12 weeks.",
 "progression": {
  "type": "DOUBLE_PROGRESSION",
  "description": "Program text: within each rep range, keep the same weight and aim for more reps each week until you have mastered it; e.g. in a 5-8 range, stay at the weight until you can do 9 reps, then go heavier but still able to do at least 5, and stay there until you can do at least 9 again. In-app week 2 note: start with last week's weights, aim for 1 more rep than before until you hit the top of the target range, then increase weight by 5-10 lb and work within the range. Each set of the pyramid progresses on its own rep range. The source gives one 5-10 lb increment for all lifts; the upper 2.5 kg / lower 5 kg split in incrementKg is a metric rounding choice for this app, not the author's.",
  "incrementKg": {
   "upper": 2.5,
   "lower": 5
  },
  "deload": "No deload or stall rule is stated by the author."
 },
